#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""needs-you-github: turn GitHub notifications and your open PRs into needs-you cards.

  needs-you-github [--dry-run] [--verbose] [--state PATH]

Run it every ~5 minutes (cron, a systemd user timer or a LaunchAgent) on one machine
that has `gh` logged in. Each run:

  1. GET /notifications (unread only), conditional on If-Modified-Since, at most once
     per X-Poll-Interval; a full refresh every 30 minutes so read threads drop off.
  2. One GraphQL query for your open PRs (review decision, mergeable, checks) and the
     open PRs that request your review.
  3. Posts a card per condition with a stable key, re-posts it while it holds (so its
     --expires-in keeps moving) and resolves it once the condition clears.
  4. When one of your PRs leaves the open list, one GraphQL lookup says whether it
     merged; if so, one `done` card "Merged owner/repo#N: title" (24 h FYI, never counted).

It shells out to `gh api`, so auth is your gh login; it never reads or prints the token.
Everything it reads from GitHub is untrusted: only titles (cleaned and truncated) and
check names reach a card; bodies and comments never do. It always exits 0.

Config (environment, else ~/.config/needs-you/env; all optional):
  NEEDS_YOU_GITHUB_INCLUDE   comma list of owner or owner/repo to watch (default: all)
  NEEDS_YOU_GITHUB_EXCLUDE   comma list of owner or owner/repo to ignore (wins over include)
  NEEDS_YOU_GITHUB_CONTEXTS  owner=work|personal,... (default NEEDS_YOU_DEFAULT_CONTEXT, else work)
  NEEDS_YOU_GITHUB_REASONS   reasons to post, comma list; "-mention,-assign" turns some off.
                             review deploy ci mention assign merge changes conflict checks merged
  NEEDS_YOU_GITHUB_INTERVAL  minutes between runs (default 5); cards expire after 3x this
  NEEDS_YOU_GITHUB_PR_DAYS   only your PRs updated in the last N days (default 14)
  NEEDS_YOU_GITHUB_MAX_CARDS at most this many cards open at once (default 20; urgent first)
  NEEDS_YOU_GITHUB_GH        path to gh (default: gh on PATH)
  NEEDS_YOU_BIN              path to the needs-you CLI (default: on PATH, else ~/.local/bin)

State: ~/.local/state/needs-you/github.json (mode 600): what it posted, Last-Modified.
Python 3.9+ standard library only.
"""
